! Performance anchor: CHF2OH, HF/6-31G(d,p), single point.
!
! This input exists to be TIMED, not to be believed. It is the system
! on which the July 2026 /heap-arrays0 regression was finally pinned
! down: 30 shells, 102265 stored shell quartets, 24.9 MB of ERI
! storage -- big enough that the integral engine dominates the wall
! clock, small enough to run in seconds on a correct build.
!
! The manifest asserts a FLOOR on the "ERI throughput: N quartets/s"
! line that v1.17.0 added after the precompute. See
! tests/manifest/30_performance.mf for why the tolerance is so wide,
! and docs/BUILD_WINDOWS_VS2019.md for what a low value means.
!
! The energy is asserted too, so that a build which is fast because it
! is wrong does not pass.
%method   hf
%basis    6-31G(d,p)
%job      energy
%charge   0
%mult     1
%print_time

%geo
H    -1.156124    0.826560    0.000000
C    -0.250166    0.202668    0.000000
F    -0.250166   -0.600957    1.146380
F    -0.250166   -0.600957   -1.146380
O     0.795568    0.974962    0.000000
H     1.568868    0.538864    0.285142
